<article class="env-definition" id="014Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/014Q">Definition <span data-tag="014Q">13.10.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category. A triangle $(X, Y, Z, f, g, h)$ of $K(\mathcal{A})$ is called a <em>distinguished triangle of $K(\mathcal{A})$</em> if it is isomorphic to the triangle associated to a termwise split exact sequence of complexes, see Definition <a href="/tag/014I" data-tag="014I">13.9.9</a>. Same definition for $K^{+}(\mathcal{A})$, $K^{-}(\mathcal{A})$, and $K^ b(\mathcal{A})$. </p>
</article>